  "contracts": [
    "Four negative/nonfinite hold inputs must produce SystemExit2 before the forbidden launch constructor, any command/material, output or sleep. Zero/default8/quarter remain valid.",
    "Two print-only cases require exact controlled absent/explicit0 environment preservation after literal shlex-decoded arguments and no launch; ambient1 is independently positive.",
    "Actual flag-enabled session must acquire, hold and clean once, then a second default session with an empty snapshot must refuse before mutation; separate default refusal and explicit ambient permission remain positive.",
    "Resources and cleanup callback exist before environment/model patches and browser/material acquisition. Every actual constructed browser is retained; independent backup attempts browser exits, original material cleanup and patch restoration, keeping unexpected failures."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All six/seven outcomes and first-oracle lines are source forecasts. Current baseline may stop at these first assertions; downstream object/command/environment assertions have no native credit.",
    "Only subprocess command results/state and sleep boundary are controlled. Actual canonical synchronous CLI/plan/session/AdbDevice logic and local temporary material run only under root execution. No ADB/device/browser, real elapsed-hold or environment-secret evidence exists.",
    "The clear=True environment uses only literal synthetic values. It temporarily replaces the process environment and is restored by registered cleanup; no inherited credential values are recorded.",
    "Lane browser/device owners are older than root: required-query/UI and async-worker ownership changes differ. The entire CLI and borrowed command model are exact; this approval is for root composition using its current owners, not unrelated old lane production.",
    "Healthy status0 behavior is modeled, and backup is finite in these controlled operations; arbitrary filesystem/OS hangs, failure during malformed backup setup, async cancellation or concurrent CLI callers are outside scope.",
    "This reviewer previously authored part of the reused lifecycle scaffold; the new thirteen-control owner has a different author. Supporting source is partial as explicitly recorded; no whole source tree/full gate/main approval.",
